# origin-config.yaml -- instance-level trust-boundary config for deploy/origin.py's F7/B6
# operator-decision-file rule (memory-engine v3, P1). GOVERNS: which raw-event FILENAME
# prefixes origin.py's assign_origin() treats as non-forgeable operator-decision files (a
# raw event named "<prefix>-*" after its date prefix mints origin: human, per B6 non-
# forgeability -- the file is pre-existing committed git history, so it predates the
# current session's run window by construction).
#
# THIS IS INSTANCE IDENTITY DATA, NOT ENGINE LOGIC: which human name(s) this instance's
# raw events are session-transcribed under. A fresh/template instance ships with NO name
# baked in here -- see the fail-safe default below.
#
# FAIL-SAFE DEFAULT (doctrine: never auto-mint human on an unresolvable config): this file
# ABSENT, PyYAML unavailable at runtime, or the content unparseable/structurally malformed
# all degrade to an EMPTY human_prefixes list -- nothing auto-mints human in that case. A
# raw event that would otherwise have matched instead falls through to origin.py's ordinary
# parseable/unmatched rule (-> corpus), or -- if the event is itself unparseable -- to
# `unknown` and the B2 operator-attestation queue. Never a silent upgrade to a MORE
# permissive origin than an unresolvable config would otherwise produce.
#
# THIS FILE IS AN OPERATOR-GATED TRUST-CONTROL SURFACE (ROUTE-1-style note, mirroring
# deploy/safe-allowlist.yaml's own convention): changing human_prefixes changes who this
# instance trusts to mint origin:human by filename alone. Treat edits as an operator-
# authored, out-of-band change only -- never something an agent/executor edits on its own
# initiative.
#
# Schema:
#   human_prefixes: [list of filename prefixes]
# Each prefix is matched case-insensitively as "^<prefix>-" against the event's basename
# AFTER its leading YYYY-MM-DD[THHMMSS]- date prefix is stripped (origin.py's own
# _stem_after_date). E.g. with human_prefixes: [alice], a raw event named
# "2026-07-05-alice-decision-9.md" matches ("alice-decision-9" starts with "alice-").
#
# Derived at init from project.yaml personnel tags (init.sh/init.ps1 section 4, personnel_tags_csv).
# Operators edit deliberately (trust-boundary; absent/malformed => nothing auto-mints human origin).

human_prefixes: [{{personnel_tags_csv}}]
